WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:46.630
CHAPTER 42:
WHY ONLY HER?

00:47.548 --> 00:49.967
What will happen if Mr. Ga finds out?

00:50.968 --> 00:53.846
Do you think you'll still
be able to talk to him like that?

00:54.764 --> 00:55.806
Drink this and cheer up.

00:59.101 --> 01:00.227
Just you wait and see, Eui-ju.

01:01.353 --> 01:02.563
You're done for.

01:04.982 --> 01:06.734
COUNSELING ROOM

01:06.817 --> 01:08.068
COUNSELING IN PROGRESS

01:12.156 --> 01:13.741
What is it you want to tell me?

01:14.575 --> 01:16.494
I've given this a lot of thought.

01:17.244 --> 01:19.038
I thought you should know, Mr. Ga.

01:21.123 --> 01:22.458
One of the girls in our class

01:23.042 --> 01:24.960
has written a novel about you.

01:26.128 --> 01:27.379
And a BL novel at that.

01:28.964 --> 01:30.674
Everyone's talking about it online.

01:32.676 --> 01:34.261
Do you know who wrote it?

01:37.431 --> 01:38.682
It was Eui-ju.

01:44.563 --> 01:45.856
I said it was Eui-ju.

01:49.902 --> 01:51.153
I know.

01:53.697 --> 01:55.199
You already knew?

01:56.158 --> 01:57.284
How…

01:59.286 --> 02:01.705
Why aren't you upset?
Doesn't it bother you?

02:02.498 --> 02:05.251
I think Eui-ju is creepy
and kind of scary.

02:06.544 --> 02:08.587
You need to read it for yourself.

02:16.095 --> 02:17.096
Wait…

02:18.138 --> 02:19.390
Have you already read it?

02:24.019 --> 02:26.021
But you haven't done anything about it?
Why not?

02:27.147 --> 02:28.524
Why, Mr. Ga?

02:29.525 --> 02:31.318
Why do you give her special treatment?

02:33.404 --> 02:34.238
What do you mean?

02:34.321 --> 02:37.032
Why do you only look out for her
and take special care of her?

02:39.201 --> 02:40.870
Why waste your energy
on someone like Eui-ju?

02:41.871 --> 02:43.747
It's not just this novel,
but after-school math too.

02:43.831 --> 02:44.832
Why only her?

02:46.876 --> 02:48.085
Mr. Ga,

02:48.669 --> 02:51.046
you don't really need to
look out for someone like her.

02:52.381 --> 02:54.258
I think you're misunderstanding something.

02:55.384 --> 02:57.052
I'm not doing this because it's Eui-ju.

02:58.637 --> 03:00.222
I would have done the same for you.

03:00.973 --> 03:03.058
Don't give me that.

03:03.809 --> 03:04.810
What I mean is,

03:04.894 --> 03:08.188
shouldn't you be looking out for me
rather than someone like her?

03:08.981 --> 03:10.441
I'm Eun Ha-su.

03:10.524 --> 03:11.901
I'm the Eun Ha-su!

03:35.007 --> 03:36.467
You're both screwed now.

03:42.431 --> 03:45.809
CHAPTER 43:
WHO IS IMUK?

03:51.732 --> 03:54.568
CHECK THIS OUT
THIS IS ABOUT OUR TEACHERS?

04:07.164 --> 04:08.749
Guys, check out this web novel.

04:08.832 --> 04:10.501
The story is about our teachers,

04:10.584 --> 04:12.586
and apparently,
the writer goes to our school.

04:18.884 --> 04:20.427
-Freaking wild, isn't it?
-Our teachers?

04:20.511 --> 04:21.929
-It's about our school.
-Really?

04:22.763 --> 04:24.473
Isn't this Mr. Ga?

04:25.849 --> 04:27.101
WE WERE FRIENDS

04:27.685 --> 04:29.395
Hey, have you seen this?

04:30.104 --> 04:31.772
This is about our teachers, right?

04:31.855 --> 04:33.607
It's crazy.

04:33.691 --> 04:36.360
Go on. Check it out already.

04:45.369 --> 04:46.620
Why are the letters so small?

04:46.704 --> 04:47.579
EPISODE 14

04:47.663 --> 04:49.123
So what's all this?

04:49.748 --> 04:50.791
It's a BL novel

04:50.874 --> 04:52.710
featuring men in a same-sex relationship.

04:52.793 --> 04:54.628
Our new teachers are the main characters.

04:55.129 --> 04:58.465
You'll see that the teachers
are portrayed as liking each other.

04:58.549 --> 05:00.467
Mr. Ga and Mr. Jung

05:00.551 --> 05:02.636
are in a love triangle with Mr. Yoon.

05:03.679 --> 05:06.223
Enough. What did I just hear?

05:06.932 --> 05:08.684
I can't say I understand
what you're saying.

05:08.767 --> 05:09.768
Oh, I feel dizzy.

05:09.852 --> 05:10.978
This is clearly defamation

05:11.061 --> 05:13.188
and a violation
of their professional rights.

05:14.189 --> 05:17.735
If this goes up on an online community
with enough traffic,

05:18.944 --> 05:20.237
it'll probably make the news.

05:20.320 --> 05:23.032
But I really don't want our school

05:23.115 --> 05:25.951
to get caught up in something so shameful.

05:27.911 --> 05:29.788
Of course not.

05:29.872 --> 05:31.707
We have to keep things
as quiet as possible

05:31.790 --> 05:33.292
and resolve things internally.

05:33.375 --> 05:34.960
Oh, my head.

05:35.044 --> 05:37.087
There's never a quiet day
in this damn place.

05:39.757 --> 05:43.510
Don't worry, I'll take care of it.
You can leave, Ha-su.

05:51.018 --> 05:52.144
What in the…

06:15.167 --> 06:16.376
It's you, isn't it?

06:17.294 --> 06:19.296
Is it really you?
Did you write that novel?

06:19.880 --> 06:21.632
Did you really write it
based on our teachers?

06:24.593 --> 06:25.511
Yeah.

06:27.096 --> 06:28.347
This is insane.

06:30.891 --> 06:33.477
-The thing is, Go-ya--
-Is that why you've been so out of it?

06:35.312 --> 06:37.940
Why didn't you say anything?
You must have felt so alone.

06:45.531 --> 06:47.699
Did you think I wouldn't understand?

06:48.951 --> 06:50.494
It's not that, Go-ya.

06:50.577 --> 06:52.204
It wasn't like that.

06:52.287 --> 06:54.414
It's not that I didn't trust you.

06:54.498 --> 06:55.415
I was…

06:58.794 --> 07:00.462
I guess I was embarrassed.

07:03.882 --> 07:05.384
I was ashamed.

07:08.178 --> 07:10.514
When I checked it out,
the views were out of this world.

07:11.098 --> 07:13.183
You said I'd be the first to know
when you hit the big time.

07:16.436 --> 07:17.604
I'm sorry.

07:20.816 --> 07:22.317
So what gave you away?

07:23.026 --> 07:24.903
How did Ha-su catch on to you?

07:27.447 --> 07:29.366
I'm not really sure.

07:30.033 --> 07:31.994
I got the feeling she'd figured it out

07:32.077 --> 07:33.412
a few days ago.

07:35.831 --> 07:38.709
My gosh, Eui-ju.

07:39.293 --> 07:40.961
Writing about our teachers?

07:41.044 --> 07:42.838
You're something else.

07:43.630 --> 07:44.715
It'll be fine.

07:45.299 --> 07:46.133
Let's go.

07:49.887 --> 07:51.388
"If you don't want to
solve these problems,

07:51.471 --> 07:52.806
you can do something else."

07:52.890 --> 07:54.016
Damn!

07:56.185 --> 07:58.770
Did you check out the comments?

08:03.192 --> 08:04.985
-Hey.
-Hey, Ha-su.

08:05.068 --> 08:07.196
How do you know Eui-ju is Imuk?
Have you got proof?

08:07.279 --> 08:08.447
Well, do you?

08:08.530 --> 08:11.325
Mr. Ga's comments from after-school math
are there word-for-word.

08:13.035 --> 08:14.244
I know you can see it too.

08:14.328 --> 08:17.039
It also contains things he said
in his very first homeroom.

08:18.207 --> 08:20.792
Let's be frank here.
Is that really such a heinous crime?

08:20.876 --> 08:22.044
So what if she is?

08:23.128 --> 08:24.338
Don't you think

08:24.963 --> 08:26.548
kids like that are a bit weird?

08:26.632 --> 08:28.258
Jeez. How creepy.

08:29.176 --> 08:31.345
Hey, everyone has different tastes.

08:31.428 --> 08:33.680
Just mind your own business.

08:33.764 --> 08:36.808
Even so, how can she write
about our teachers like that?

08:37.601 --> 08:41.271
Imagine if she writes about us
like that behind our backs?

08:41.355 --> 08:43.106
She might even be writing right now.

08:43.190 --> 08:44.441
Some lesbian crap about our school.

08:45.400 --> 08:46.610
That's so freaky.

08:46.693 --> 08:49.112
Freaks like her would insist
it's a matter of freedom of speech

08:49.196 --> 08:50.697
but then go on to become criminals.

08:51.281 --> 08:52.115
Hey, you…

08:56.495 --> 08:57.829
I guess we can ask her directly.

08:59.831 --> 09:01.875
-There you are, Eui-ju.
-Hey, Eui-ju.

09:01.959 --> 09:02.793
Morning.

09:03.835 --> 09:05.087
-Good morning.
-Yeah.

09:08.757 --> 09:12.010
If the disciplinary committee is involved,
your parents will be told.

09:12.886 --> 09:14.721
If my parents ever read
the BL novel I wrote,

09:15.639 --> 09:17.266
I'm running away pronto.

09:17.349 --> 09:18.934
-True that.
-For sure.

09:19.017 --> 09:20.894
I'd want to disappear
off the face of the earth.

09:20.978 --> 09:22.646
-Fair enough.
-It's that bad.

09:23.397 --> 09:24.940
Damn it, you crazy bitch!

09:35.158 --> 09:36.118
-Stop it!
-Hey!

09:37.953 --> 09:39.204
What's going on here?

10:08.191 --> 10:09.067
Eui-ju,

10:10.610 --> 10:11.445
come with me.

10:20.996 --> 10:21.997
-Hey.
-What?

10:22.080 --> 10:23.999
-What are you doing?
-Stop it.

10:24.082 --> 10:25.584
-Stop it!
-Hey!

10:25.667 --> 10:26.877
-Why, you…
-Stop it, will you?

10:26.960 --> 10:32.132
CHAPTER 44: YOU MUST TAKE RESPONSIBILITY
FOR YOUR ACTIONS

10:49.232 --> 10:50.067
Mr. Ga.

10:52.194 --> 10:54.404
Just pretend you didn't know.

10:57.199 --> 10:59.951
I don't want you getting in trouble
because of me.

11:03.538 --> 11:06.249
Shouldn't you be worrying about yourself?

11:06.958 --> 11:09.544
It's only right
that I take responsibility.

11:11.046 --> 11:12.589
So, you can

11:12.672 --> 11:13.673
just…

11:14.508 --> 11:15.717
say you didn't know.

11:17.302 --> 11:18.553
Okay?

11:18.637 --> 11:20.097
You have to.

11:20.180 --> 11:23.183
We'll say you didn't know anything,
just like the other teachers.

11:24.017 --> 11:26.603
This was all my own doing.

11:27.938 --> 11:28.897
So,

11:30.065 --> 11:33.151
it has nothing to do with you, sir.

11:38.532 --> 11:40.409
You'll have to face
the disciplinary committee.

11:41.618 --> 11:44.996
Think about what you're going to say
and how you'll take responsibility,

11:45.872 --> 11:47.040
and prepare well.

11:50.252 --> 11:51.420
Yes, sir.

11:53.422 --> 11:54.756
I will take responsibility too.

11:56.216 --> 11:58.385
I'm partly responsible, for sure.

11:59.928 --> 12:02.848
But you'll have to take responsibility
for your part. That's unavoidable.

12:05.976 --> 12:08.019
Yes, sir. I know.

12:09.563 --> 12:10.772
I'm sure you're scared.

12:11.731 --> 12:13.608
You're probably full of regret
and embarrassed too.

12:14.109 --> 12:15.777
It might feel like
everything is crumbling down.

12:17.070 --> 12:19.072
But this doesn't mean your life is over.

12:20.407 --> 12:22.534
It might feel like that right now,

12:23.368 --> 12:24.703
but it's not.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.835
I don't know how things will turn out.

12:32.544 --> 12:34.337
But what matters more than the results,

12:34.421 --> 12:37.382
is how you comport yourself
during the process, accept it,

12:38.091 --> 12:39.342
and deal with it.

12:40.552 --> 12:41.970
Do you get what I'm saying?

12:44.473 --> 12:45.515
Yes, sir.

12:51.396 --> 12:53.440
The principal wants to see you. Let's go.

12:59.404 --> 13:00.530
What is this?

13:01.156 --> 13:03.158
What on earth is this? The teachers…

13:05.202 --> 13:07.496
How dare you make your teachers
characters in a novel?

13:07.579 --> 13:09.164
You. A student!

13:09.748 --> 13:12.375
This is unacceptable.

13:12.459 --> 13:14.377
Ms. Kim, the thing is…

13:15.378 --> 13:17.672
What do you take this school for?
And your teachers?

13:17.756 --> 13:19.299
How dare you? You, a student!

13:19.382 --> 13:21.551
A student mocking teachers
and turning them into a joke…

13:21.635 --> 13:23.803
Is this what education has become?

13:25.013 --> 13:27.516
What on earth
are the kids of today learning?

13:27.599 --> 13:29.809
Making fools out of their teachers.

13:31.269 --> 13:32.812
Delete it immediately!

13:32.896 --> 13:34.564
Wipe it from the Internet.

13:34.648 --> 13:36.983
What will happen to the school's
reputation if parents find out?

13:38.235 --> 13:41.446
It's an absolute disgrace.

13:42.155 --> 13:43.532
I'm sorry.

13:44.658 --> 13:47.452
Ms. Kim, may I add something? Actually--

13:47.536 --> 13:50.038
If you have something to say,
save it for the hearing.

13:50.121 --> 13:52.332
Make sure Eui-ju's parents attend.

13:52.415 --> 13:53.542
And the other teachers too.

13:53.625 --> 13:55.794
The ones in the novel.

13:55.877 --> 13:58.463
Mr. Yoon, Mr. Jung, and Mr. Noh.

14:03.677 --> 14:04.803
Yes, ma'am.

14:06.680 --> 14:08.098
I'll see that she's expelled.

14:08.181 --> 14:10.559
This is completely unacceptable!

14:16.481 --> 14:18.108
MALE TEACHERS' LOUNGE

14:31.830 --> 14:32.872
What is this?

14:35.834 --> 14:38.545
Wow, your reading comprehension
is really something else.

14:40.338 --> 14:42.257
Listen carefully.

14:44.092 --> 14:45.385
You and him,

14:46.052 --> 14:47.721
and him and Woo-su

14:48.305 --> 14:50.473
are involved-involved.
Let me put it this way.

14:50.557 --> 14:53.184
That kid let her imagination
run dangerously wild

14:53.268 --> 14:55.395
and came up with a delusional fiction.

14:55.478 --> 14:57.147
Why were we paired up anyway?

15:00.942 --> 15:02.861
Just forget it.

15:03.737 --> 15:04.571
But…

15:05.864 --> 15:07.324
Letter girl, that brat!

15:07.407 --> 15:09.909
What did I tell you
about that weird glint in her eyes?

15:09.993 --> 15:11.745
I'm a great judge of character, you know.

15:14.831 --> 15:17.334
How long are you going
to keep reading that?

15:17.417 --> 15:20.879
So, is this a matter
of freedom of expression

15:20.962 --> 15:22.297
or invasion of privacy?

15:23.673 --> 15:24.924
Should we do something?

15:25.008 --> 15:26.801
Is this something we should sue over?

15:27.427 --> 15:28.720
Okay, shall I call a lawyer?

15:28.803 --> 15:31.139
What should we sue her for?

15:31.222 --> 15:32.599
Defamation.

15:32.682 --> 15:34.559
Hey, kids are gonna mess around.

15:34.643 --> 15:35.727
Man, this guy's trouble.

15:35.810 --> 15:37.187
That's a dangerous take.

15:37.854 --> 15:39.648
This isn't something
we should just let go.

15:39.731 --> 15:40.857
See.

15:40.940 --> 15:41.775
No?

15:41.858 --> 15:44.486
She quoted us verbatim
without our permission.

15:44.986 --> 15:46.905
The things we said and did.

15:47.530 --> 15:49.366
Since she didn't ask our permission,

15:49.449 --> 15:51.618
if we've suffered any damages,

15:51.701 --> 15:53.036
we can sue her in civil court.

15:53.119 --> 15:54.204
Yeah.

15:54.913 --> 15:58.667
There's no clear rule about the boundary
between real life and fiction,

15:59.501 --> 16:01.336
but questions will arise
on the author's ethics.

16:02.045 --> 16:02.879
Wow.

16:03.713 --> 16:06.299
See? By the way, why are you being

16:06.383 --> 16:07.884
a fierce tiger baring its teeth,

16:07.967 --> 16:11.554
instead of the cuddly pussycat
you normally are?

16:12.555 --> 16:13.723
However,

16:15.225 --> 16:17.477
if we acknowledge
we haven't suffered any harm,

16:17.560 --> 16:19.062
then there's no real issue.

16:19.896 --> 16:21.481
So basically,

16:22.440 --> 16:24.317
Eui-ju's punishment hinges on what we say?

16:24.401 --> 16:25.276
Yeah.

16:33.201 --> 16:34.452
What did the principal say?

16:35.078 --> 16:36.329
She's going crazy, right?

16:37.747 --> 16:38.790
There'll be a hearing.

16:39.958 --> 16:41.126
She wants you guys to attend.

16:43.336 --> 16:47.090
According to Dong-ju, the published author
with a degree in Korean Education,

16:47.173 --> 16:48.758
our opinion on the matter

16:48.842 --> 16:51.803
would affect the punishment
for that little brat, Eui-ju.

16:51.886 --> 16:52.887
What are you going to do?

16:56.266 --> 16:58.143
How should she be punished?

17:00.019 --> 17:04.566
Woo-su, use that brilliant mind of yours
to come up with a cruel punishment.

17:04.649 --> 17:06.568
-Hey.
-What?

17:09.654 --> 17:11.156
We should each make our own decision.

17:23.042 --> 17:24.127
Are you okay?

17:28.506 --> 17:29.758
Don't worry about the others.

17:30.425 --> 17:32.302
It'll all blow over in a week or so.

18:04.375 --> 18:05.376
Oh, Dad.

18:05.460 --> 18:08.213
Hey, baby. Fancy seeing you here.

18:09.088 --> 18:10.173
There's no need.

18:11.216 --> 18:13.635
Why do you look so down? Are you sick?

18:14.344 --> 18:15.887
No, it's just that

18:16.554 --> 18:17.889
I'm a bit tired.

18:18.890 --> 18:21.726
Are you okay?
You've been doing a lot of overtime.

18:21.810 --> 18:22.769
True.

18:22.852 --> 18:24.687
Drawing up the budget.

18:25.355 --> 18:27.315
Dealing with residents' complaints.

18:27.398 --> 18:28.483
My goodness.

18:29.734 --> 18:32.779
But as soon as I see your face,

18:32.862 --> 18:35.198
all the stress melts away.

18:35.281 --> 18:36.950
Away it goes.

18:43.206 --> 18:44.582
Is it because of all the studying?

18:45.250 --> 18:46.543
Shall I buy you an ice cream?

18:46.626 --> 18:48.086
No, I'm okay.

18:56.511 --> 18:57.345
Kid.

18:59.347 --> 19:00.723
Let me give you some dad wisdom.

19:01.349 --> 19:03.268
After living a fair few years now,

19:04.269 --> 19:06.563
I realized that life

19:06.646 --> 19:10.650
is about carrying a lot of worries
with you wherever you go.

19:11.818 --> 19:13.987
I guess that's to be expected.

19:15.071 --> 19:16.447
So whatever happens in your life,

19:17.615 --> 19:18.950
don't worry too much.

19:22.620 --> 19:23.621
Okay.

19:25.790 --> 19:28.084
I don't know
what you're worrying about these days,

19:29.168 --> 19:32.130
but it probably feels like
the biggest thing in the world.

19:32.881 --> 19:34.591
And of course, that's understandable.

19:34.674 --> 19:35.925
When I was your age,

19:36.801 --> 19:40.054
I felt like the world
was collapsing around me every day.

19:41.055 --> 19:43.725
But looking back,

19:44.350 --> 19:47.687
all those things
I bawled my eyes out over…

19:48.438 --> 19:50.982
Turned out to be nothing?

19:51.608 --> 19:53.026
No.

19:53.109 --> 19:55.820
I'd be lying if I said they were nothing.

19:56.738 --> 19:58.948
But looking back,

20:00.617 --> 20:01.868
like pieces of armor,

20:02.493 --> 20:05.788
they stuck to me here and there

20:06.789 --> 20:09.000
and made me stronger.

20:10.710 --> 20:11.669
So, Eui-ju,

20:12.754 --> 20:15.423
just go at your own pace.

20:16.507 --> 20:19.469
Don't rush or push yourself too hard.

20:20.136 --> 20:22.263
Rest when you need to.

20:23.222 --> 20:25.141
I'll stay right by your side

20:25.683 --> 20:27.143
so that when you're tired,

20:27.226 --> 20:30.688
I can bring you
a nice cold glass of water.

20:35.276 --> 20:36.694
Even if things are rough now,

20:37.487 --> 20:38.988
they will work out in the end.

20:39.906 --> 20:40.782
Honestly, they will.

20:41.658 --> 20:44.035
I've seen it for myself.

20:50.792 --> 20:51.918
Dad, I…

20:53.503 --> 20:54.504
To tell the truth,

20:55.296 --> 20:57.090
there's something I need to tell you.

21:02.512 --> 21:03.680
CHAPTER 45:
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

21:03.763 --> 21:04.806
What does she want to say?

21:05.348 --> 21:07.475
I don't know. Let's wait and see.

21:22.407 --> 21:23.825
Why are you doing that?

21:24.450 --> 21:25.702
What's this?

21:25.785 --> 21:27.787
If you stay like that,
you'll hurt your knees.

21:27.870 --> 21:28.705
Get up.

21:28.788 --> 21:30.665
Mom, Dad. I write novels online.

21:33.418 --> 21:34.335
Novels?

21:36.421 --> 21:37.797
I was in eighth grade

21:38.923 --> 21:39.841
when I first started.

21:43.219 --> 21:44.554
Nobody ever reads them.

21:46.097 --> 21:47.473
But I enjoyed it.

21:50.143 --> 21:51.436
Writing novels

21:51.519 --> 21:54.105
and seeing the characters
I created come to life

21:54.731 --> 21:55.940
was so exciting.

21:57.108 --> 21:59.694
So I kept writing.

22:00.987 --> 22:03.906
Even when I didn't want to get up
in the morning or go to school,

22:03.990 --> 22:06.617
just thinking about writing at night
gave me such a thrill.

22:07.827 --> 22:08.661
I…

22:10.747 --> 22:13.458
I know I'm not much good at anything.

22:14.876 --> 22:16.627
And what's more,

22:17.295 --> 22:18.796
I never particularly enjoyed anything.

22:19.964 --> 22:21.549
But for the first time ever,

22:23.217 --> 22:24.886
I found something I really enjoyed.

22:26.763 --> 22:27.680
And that was…

22:29.390 --> 22:30.725
writing novels.

22:33.227 --> 22:35.104
Writing novels of all things.

22:37.982 --> 22:39.525
I wonder who you take after.

22:41.152 --> 22:41.986
So,

22:43.029 --> 22:44.280
what's the problem?

22:45.615 --> 22:47.742
My latest work

22:47.825 --> 22:50.244
was really popular.

22:50.328 --> 22:52.830
It got a huge number of views and likes.

22:52.914 --> 22:56.375
And a famous publisher
agreed to launch it.

22:56.959 --> 22:58.377
That's amazing.

22:58.461 --> 23:00.671
I'm so proud of you, my girl!

23:00.755 --> 23:01.798
But the thing is…

23:03.966 --> 23:06.928
the story was all about my teachers.

23:12.725 --> 23:13.976
I based my main characters

23:15.436 --> 23:18.523
on my teachers.

23:20.316 --> 23:22.401
People at school found out.

23:24.779 --> 23:27.156
And now the principal
wants to hold a disciplinary hearing.

23:27.240 --> 23:28.074
What?

23:29.117 --> 23:30.952
This is my novel.

23:31.702 --> 23:33.955
I'm sorry.
Wait until I'm in my room to read it.

23:42.338 --> 23:45.341
Why hold a disciplinary hearing
over a novel?

23:46.342 --> 23:48.010
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

24:01.649 --> 24:07.071
WE WERE FRIENDS
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

24:11.492 --> 24:14.954
Hello, this is Imuk.

24:16.122 --> 24:19.667
I wrote We Were Friends using traits

24:19.750 --> 24:21.586
of real people around me as inspiration.

24:22.670 --> 24:26.215
I dissected aspects of their daily life,
their way of speaking, and their habits,

24:26.299 --> 24:30.636
and arbitrarily adapted them for my story.

24:31.762 --> 24:33.222
As a writer,

24:33.973 --> 24:36.017
I should've created something of my own,

24:36.100 --> 24:37.435
but I couldn't.

24:39.145 --> 24:41.063
I sincerely apologize.

24:42.273 --> 24:45.985
I've only now realized
that my writing caused discomfort

24:46.068 --> 24:49.280
and hurt to others.

24:50.781 --> 24:53.701
I sincerely apologize.

24:57.121 --> 25:00.541
Writing this story made me very happy.

25:00.625 --> 25:02.126
I felt excited.

25:03.044 --> 25:06.964
But that happiness was built
by borrowing from others,

25:07.048 --> 25:08.925
no, by taking from them

25:09.008 --> 25:11.177
without their permission.

25:11.260 --> 25:13.846
WE WERE FRIENDS

25:13.930 --> 25:18.059
To take responsibility for my actions,
I will be deleting this novel.

25:19.143 --> 25:21.395
If the day ever comes
when I can write again,

25:22.480 --> 25:23.814
I will think, reflect,

25:23.898 --> 25:26.025
and imagine on my own,

25:26.901 --> 25:29.278
so I can write something truly mine.

25:31.989 --> 25:33.574
Thank you for reading.

25:35.034 --> 25:36.244
I was so very grateful.

25:36.327 --> 25:38.996
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

25:42.500 --> 25:44.001
Be it hate comments,

25:44.710 --> 25:45.670
no comments,

25:46.504 --> 25:48.339
my lack of skill,

25:48.422 --> 25:50.466
or the ridicule of those around me,

25:51.092 --> 25:53.928
I thought nothing could stop me
from writing.

25:55.221 --> 25:56.722
I believed

25:57.848 --> 26:00.101
I could always keep writing

26:00.726 --> 26:02.853
and that I always would, no matter what.

26:05.398 --> 26:06.816
But now,

26:08.526 --> 26:09.485
I can no longer…

26:09.568 --> 26:11.946
DO YOU WANT TO DELETE THIS NOVEL?

26:14.907 --> 26:16.742
…be the same as I was before.

26:16.826 --> 26:23.666
"WE WERE FRIENDS" HAS BEEN DELETED
RETURN TO MY TITLES

26:27.753 --> 26:28.713
We are gathered today

26:28.796 --> 26:32.049
to discuss the novel written by Yeo Eui-ju
featuring her teachers as characters.

26:32.133 --> 26:34.677
We won't necessarily take your side.

26:34.760 --> 26:37.096
I believe if Eui-ju hopes to keep writing,

26:37.179 --> 26:38.597
she needs to learn something from this.

26:38.681 --> 26:39.515
She must be expelled!

26:39.598 --> 26:41.058
I told her to keep writing.

26:41.142 --> 26:42.435
I'm the one who's responsible.

26:42.518 --> 26:45.271
Mr. Ga won't be able to come to school
for the time being.

26:45.354 --> 26:46.731
How bad is it?

26:46.814 --> 26:48.816
He didn't want to tell you
for fear you'd worry.

26:48.899 --> 26:51.360
Mr. Ga, why did you do it?

26:52.611 --> 26:53.696
To me, you're…

26:55.948 --> 26:56.949
You're…

27:55.674 --> 27:57.676
Subtitle: Paul Carver
